@cucooOnGithub The labs should be able to provide basic PII and privacy by default rather than having us to rely on system prompts, skills, or proxies as crutches for their incompetence and their inability to follow basic security "don't leak my data" practices. 

It's nice to use a proxy anyway, and its great that its free. But you are building a free tool to monkeypatch the glaring bugs in the flagship product of a supposedly `1.5` trillion $ company _(I hear that number's gone down a notch recently, and I wont be surprised if it goes down further)_! Why don't THEY fix it? Why did it happen in the first place? What is the next thing that they gonna slop and leak? 

The quality bar is already dangerously low, with us giving them a pass on each and every blunder they make and us building our own tools to cope with their blunders, that just makes the bar go underground.
